{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.conversion",
    "description": "Template library: the two conversions that stand between an emission FACTOR and an emission MASS — docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §4.4 (unitcf.f) and §4.7 (`temporal_scale`).\n\nunitcf.f dispatches on an EMISSION-rate unit code, and each arm returns a DIFFERENT unit: `hp` for g/hp-hr (it converts g/hp-hr to g/hr by multiplying by hpavg x faclod, exhaust.rs:228-236), `gal/h` for g/gallon (bsfc x faclod x hpavg / density), and a dimensionless 1 for the pass-throughs (g/hr, g/day, MULT, and g/gallon when the ACTIVITY is already in gallons). A single template selecting among them cannot be typed: under esm-spec §4.8.6 every branch of an `ifelse` must agree, and an `hp` arm beside a bare 1 is a mismatch. So each arm that needs arithmetic is its own template and the code is fixed at the call site, which knows it -- every call site in this repository is a g/hp-hr rate and applies `hp_hour_unit_conversion`, typed `hp`. `gallon_unit_conversion` is the g/gallon arm, returning `gal/h` from a `lb/(hp*h)` BSFC and a `lb/gal` density; no RunSpec in this repository reaches it, and it carries unitcf.f's zero-density guard, which returns 0 rather than dividing. A pass-through arm is the identity and needs no template. (docs/esm-conventions.md §105 supersedes §58.3, which put a multi-unit selector here and the unit at the call site.)\n\nThe activity-unit codes are this file's own `enums` block, read by zero-parameter constant-fragment templates (esm-spec §9.6.1). The `enum` ops resolve against THIS file's block and never the importer's (esm-spec §9.3, §9.7.5; docs/esm-conventions.md §6, finding F3, retired at EarthSciAST PR #341), so an importer needs no copy of them. `activity_unit` is modyr.rs:75-86's ActivityUnits exactly (1-4).\n\n`annual_activity_hours` is modyr.rs:78-88's acttmp, which converts an activity level to annual hours according to its ACTIVITY-unit code: hours-per-year passes through, hours-per-day multiplies by 365 (the `per year` and `per day` name an accounting period, so both are `h`), and either gallons code becomes 1/(2*uselif). That last arm is NONROAD's own: a reciprocal of hours that the Fortran then reads as hours. It is written `1 h / (2 x (uselif / 1 h))` -- the number the Fortran computes, stated in the unit it is used as -- so all three arms are `h` and the selection is checked; dividing and multiplying by 1.0 changes no bit.\n\n`temporal_scale` carries a trap worth naming: the 7x and the 1/ndays enter the engine's product SEPARATELY (adjustment_time = 1/ndays inside emstmp, tpltmp2 = mthf*dayf outside), and combining them wrongly double-applies the monthly factor — a ~2.6x error for a 31-day month, spelled out at moves.rs executor.rs:1513-1519. They are one template here so that they are applied once, together, in one place. The three temporal factors are pure numbers and stay `1`: `month_fraction` and `day_fraction` are fractions of an activity total, and the 7 and the days-in-month are COUNTS of days, so their ratio is dimensionless and the annual-to-typical-day scale is a fraction rather than a rate.\n\n`short_tons_per_gram` is CVTTON (consts.rs:355), the unit the engine accumulates in, and `grams_per_short_ton` is its inverse, which the output stage applies (nonroad_loader.rs:2177) -- one constant, defined once, so the round trip cannot drift. BOTH DECLARE THEIR UNIT (docs/esm-conventions.md §58): `short_ton/g` on CVTTON, and a `units: \"1\"` on the numerator of its inverse, because `1.0 / const(short_ton/g)` with a BARE one is undeterminable and the inverse would then check nothing -- measured, `out_emissionQuant` declared `short_ton` is silent with the bare one and refused with the declared one.\n\n`hours_per_day` is the 24 the hour-of-day axis wraps at: `TankTemperatureGenerator` TTG-1a interpolates hour `h` toward hour `h + 1` and hour 24 toward hour 1, and the wrap is the only place in that step where a literal could be written and be wrong without any test noticing, because hour 24 is one row of 24. It is here rather than in `lib/evaporative.esm` because it is a property of the clock, not of the evaporative chain. `default_month_fraction` and `default_day_fraction` are canonical's defmth = 1/12 and defday = 1/7 (nonroad_loader.rs:2273-2288): the fallbacks when an SCC's ladder finds no allocation row at all, and NOT a neutral 1.0.\n\n`printed_decimal` is a number as MOVES PRINTS it into a NONROAD input file: `%10.3f` is `printed_decimal(x, 1000)`, half-up as Java's `Formatter` rounds. NONROAD reads the printed value, not the table's, so where a file's format has fewer decimals than the table the model reads the printed one -- the SEASON file's monthly fractions are the case that matters (PLAN.md 7.3.37). Evaluated in binary32 it agrees with Java's decimal half-up on every row of both month allocation tables, the three that sit exactly on a half included.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "nonroad", "units", "temporal", "template-library"]
  },
  "enums": {
    "activity_unit": { "HoursPerYear": 1, "HoursPerDay": 2, "GallonsPerYear": 3, "GallonsPerDay": 4 }
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "activity_unit_hours_per_year": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "enum", "args": ["activity_unit", "HoursPerYear"] } },
    "activity_unit_hours_per_day": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "enum", "args": ["activity_unit", "HoursPerDay"] } },
    "activity_unit_gallons_per_year": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "enum", "args": ["activity_unit", "GallonsPerYear"] } },
    "activity_unit_gallons_per_day": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "enum", "args": ["activity_unit", "GallonsPerDay"] } },
    "days_per_week": { "params": [], "body": 7.0 },
    "hours_per_day": { "params": [], "body": 24.0 },
    "short_tons_per_gram": { "params": [], "body":
      { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.102311e-06, "units": "short_ton/g" } },
    "grams_per_short_ton": {
      "params": [],
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0, "units": "1" },
        { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "short_tons_per_gram", "bindings": {} }] }
    },
    "days_per_year": { "params": [], "body": 365.0 },
    "printed_decimal": { "params": ["value", "scale"], "body": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "floor", "args": [{ "op": "+", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["value", "scale"] }, 0.5] }] }, "scale"] } },
    "opt_option_value": {
      "description": "The value NONROAD reads back from one line of the .OPT file's /OPTIONS/ packet, for a value in [0, 10). MOVES writes it with DecimalFormat(\"0.00000000\") after the 21-character label (NonroadOptFileHelper.java), and rdnropt.f reads it with `read(line(21:30),'(F10.0)')`: the separating space and the first NINE characters of the number. So it is rounded to eight decimals and then CUT to seven. That costs a weight-percent sulfur most of its digits: 0.00066419126 is written 0.00066419 and read 0.0006641. The rounding stays an integer count of 1e-8 before it is cut, so that binary32 never rounds a written 0.0006642 to 6641.9999 below the cut.",
      "params": ["value"],
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "floor", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "floor", "args": [{ "op": "+", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["value", 1.0e8] }, 0.5] }] }, 10.0] }] }, 1.0e7] }
    },
    "default_month_fraction": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "/", "args": [1.0, 12.0] } },
    "default_day_fraction": { "params": [], "body": { "op": "/", "args": [1.0, 7.0] } },
    "annual_activity_hours": {
      "params": ["activity_level", "activity_unit_code", "median_life_full_load"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": "==", "args": ["activity_unit_code",
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "activity_unit_hours_per_year", "bindings": {} }] },
          "activity_level",
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              { "op": "==", "args": ["activity_unit_code",
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "activity_unit_hours_per_day", "bindings": {} }] },
              { "op": "*", "args": ["activity_level",
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "days_per_year", "bindings": {} }] },
              { "op": "/", "args": [
                { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0, "units": "h" },
                { "op": "*", "args": [2.0,
                  { "op": "/", "args": ["median_life_full_load", { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0, "units": "h" }] }] }] }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "hp_hour_unit_conversion": {
      "params": ["hp_avg", "load_factor"],
      "body": { "op": "*", "args": ["hp_avg", "load_factor"] }
    },
    "gallon_unit_conversion": {
      "params": ["bsfc", "load_factor", "hp_avg", "fuel_density"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": "==", "args": ["fuel_density", 0.0] },
          0.0,
          { "op": "/", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": ["bsfc", "load_factor", "hp_avg"] },
            "fuel_density"] }
        ]
      }
    },
    "temporal_scale": {
      "params": ["month_fraction", "day_fraction", "days_in_month"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "month_fraction",
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "days_per_week", "bindings": {} },
              "day_fraction"
            ]
          },
          "days_in_month"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
